/-!
# Trust-boundary census for the compact activation traces

The activation traces and their label projections depend on no certificate, so their census
entries are kept apart from `Action/TrustBoundary.lean`, whose own imports reach the Action
certificates and so cost hours to elaborate. Splitting them means a change to the trace layer can
be census-checked in seconds.

The `+choice` entries are the definitions that name a `Gate`: Clean's `Gate.withSelector` itself
depends on `Classical.choice`, so every activation form inherits it, while the selector forms
carry only numeric indices and stay choice-free.
-/

